5487703,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7JynFX","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T11:42:55Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T11:42:55Z","body":"Then it might be a wrong design 😃? There is no StaticBody on my cube, so I would expect Godot to use the origin as a reference. As a level designer, I place my origin so that my objects integrate well with the level. In fact, most of the time, I want my objects to be slightly underground.\n\nI would say the design could be:\n- if there is a PhysicsBody, keep current behaviour (using collision check)\n- if there is no PhysicsBody, use origin to place the object on the ground\n- allow to swap between one behaviour or the other with a modifier key\n- add a setting in Project Setting to choose default behaviour in both case\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3385487703/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"ht